{"type":"message","id":"310db0e9","parentId":"9baad314","timestamp":"2026-04-22T13:42:03.973Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Calculating audio statistics**\n\nI need to get some basic audio statistics using wave and audioop. My focus will be on computing the duration and the root mean square (RMS) by chunk. I’m also considering checking the proportion of silence in the audio, which could add some valuable insight. There seems to be a lot I can explore here, and it’s important to get this right for whoever needs the information! Let's go step by step.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_017d8e8ae2d554ef0169e8d02242b481918860e6e71d94396f\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp6NAkY26dKGPTamzpCWhtvB9y3czJ_O6cqvNfsKV0QX1myHDsMJJkQZCs6O_hJz459gtdiAwvIX6mwyjKS86JbhOJS6plXli-Ovpa6yti2844ZbFfHw5BJMb1pK5mV5GN-4OJyOAzH7Y5pzQjC7Qc-V3zwBhVDMD3iZ9NUa_I7qPWfyWQxuMDdWn7nGombYFZnEOmSziqgyfigO3z2FoSDKXs-fo5zdKYL3_kfGFsj2z5_3Hd1fcMFbJSFa585EVYYUbgxdWY-9LJEXQyQ7idiIoaZ457dfiKBbix6ZPKHgW3ZXQ428iP5it3RYMQaO0Wt6SCjh2GMOtp4Y-Q8YNIDGaYWKtO26LccztQYQoY9PfpY3YjSopVsI7He2wvSpnSAXosTdLd_eA6ya9buVFyzwDxOyTKsUwo0sJ8g2VX7wGKR2Tgvkf2CKmgtj5CAsrSS66EGxy6QxTXLmMYXM8FKS59FcPkFIDH653ppr-LCvjKjYqz5cwBbtXeZLfqnWZ-EY8ionpM6X0IXXiQgYnFNJbbucVRAkdrCxAVpRDDzSAu-zyKbORLlz6v_a-od5DWkzIb-0QmybJHm1J0GqZCcd8azbOWyTSfz4Vs5Uz5kjdbyoHFsc8ZNH2UprxhNhSkvb-5YUK9sFKJqv6-Cm-EMSU7Rhx89JeF65izZ-Q9jTd3QSf6xrIQrhgRbbkOYO4qsgGXD7QENvA-gZp5BuMGYwMBrIEP-ddgOp9Ux6Wy1G6FIk5NJe7XRH9bGe1YDFJwecAIU6K32RufgTCUfcD2MRKqGSyAnVL8J12GTaz7MxGERzEEyZWx6rTesWIX4GkTHw9FXeDTQFScscxJ0Clw1-C29O9T4isE1qJRp2c63q6GgI489K2v4I3661FeXbb5S0aNflOnetCnMDeOZI7X5YhT8prXuE5WPUhlwi0IRxsfYaiTYhuSt_xim7Ji8bsTnK2Qek30OhNfxWygZP7hB4U0eAEVfI6_rxlHh7U24lzpKjDMZ_2cYy1d2dfYudLdQsfcnowSJhloxAN6TCorG_MKPcejJM0_XyzOqogWJJPY6lg=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Calculating audio statistics**\\n\\nI need to get some basic audio statistics using wave and audioop. My focus will be on computing the duration and the root mean square (RMS) by chunk. I’m also considering checking the proportion of silence in the audio, which could add some valuable insight. There seems to be a lot I can explore here, and it’s important to get this right for whoever needs the information! Let's go step by step.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_vD2Nr3xyjbe9oBtBSbYy5Vdy|fc_017d8e8ae2d554ef0169e8d02452f48191924ab0d50982d78b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport wave, audioop, contextlib, math\np='/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/Patient_Depressed---e805633c-88d2-48b0-9db0-cece8f300d20.wav'\nwith contextlib.closing(wave.open(p,'rb')) as w:\n    fr=w.getframerate(); sw=w.getsampwidth(); ch=w.getnchannels(); n=w.getnframes()\n    win=int(fr*0.5)\n    rms=[]; zc=[]\n    prev=None\n    for i in range(0,n,win):\n        frames=w.readframes(min(win,n-i))\n        if ch==2:\n            frames=audioop.tomono(frames,sw,0.5,0.5)\n        r=audioop.rms(frames,sw)\n        rms.append(r)\n        # crude zero crossings\n        samples=audioop.lin2lin(frames,sw,2)\n        count=0\n        last=None\n        for j in range(0,len(samples),2):\n            s=int.from_bytes(samples[j:j+2],'little',signed=True)\n            sign=s>=0\n            if last is not None and sign!=last:\n                count+=1\n            last=sign\n        zc.append(count)\n    mx=max(rms) if rms else 0\n    sil=sum(1 for r in rms if r < mx*0.1)\n    print('windows',len(rms),'max_rms',mx,'mean_rms',round(sum(rms)/len(rms),1),'min_rms',min(rms))\n    print('silence_windows',sil,'silence_ratio',round(sil/len(rms),2))\n    print('rms_first10',rms[:10])\n    print('rms_last10',rms[-10:])\n    print('zc_mean',round(sum(zc)/len(zc),1),'zc_min',min(zc),'zc_max',max(zc))\nPY","yieldMs":10000,"workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent-2"},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport wave, audioop, contextlib, math\\np='/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/Patient_Depressed---e805633c-88d2-48b0-9db0-cece8f300d20.wav'\\nwith contextlib.closing(wave.open(p,'rb')) as w:\\n    fr=w.getframerate(); sw=w.getsampwidth(); ch=w.getnchannels(); n=w.getnframes()\\n    win=int(fr*0.5)\\n    rms=[]; zc=[]\\n    prev=None\\n    for i in range(0,n,win):\\n        frames=w.readframes(min(win,n-i))\\n        if ch==2:\\n            frames=audioop.tomono(frames,sw,0.5,0.5)\\n        r=audioop.rms(frames,sw)\\n        rms.append(r)\\n        # crude zero crossings\\n        samples=audioop.lin2lin(frames,sw,2)\\n        count=0\\n        last=None\\n        for j in range(0,len(samples),2):\\n            s=int.from_bytes(samples[j:j+2],'little',signed=True)\\n            sign=s>=0\\n            if last is not None and sign!=last:\\n                count+=1\\n            last=sign\\n        zc.append(count)\\n    mx=max(rms) if rms else 0\\n    sil=sum(1 for r in rms if r < mx*0.1)\\n    print('windows',len(rms),'max_rms',mx,'mean_rms',round(sum(rms)/len(rms),1),'min_rms',min(rms))\\n    print('silence_windows',sil,'silence_ratio',round(sil/len(rms),2))\\n    print('rms_first10',rms[:10])\\n    print('rms_last10',rms[-10:])\\n    print('zc_mean',round(sum(zc)/len(zc),1),'zc_min',min(zc),'zc_max',max(zc))\\nPY\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent-2\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1022,"output":526,"cacheRead":7168,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8716,"cost":{"input":0.0025550000000000004,"output":0.00789,"cacheRead":0.001792,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.012237}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776865313035,"responseId":"resp_017d8e8ae2d554ef0169e8d02162b48191930a900bd4814655"}}
